                        "form": "рыбаре́"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "56e317b4-ede1-49a2-b6a1-29d3f6399f3c",
                        "entry_id": "1811f407-04b5-3f47-986b-39c2bb483a30",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "рыбаря́х"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7155259-c3d7-3f2c-844e-beafa180d228",
                        "entry_id": "1811f407-04b5-3f47-986b-39c2bb483a30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что рыбак"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8480093-fe67-4f38-99a2-62642acdf6c3",
                                "sense_id": "e7155259-c3d7-3f2c-844e-beafa180d228",
                                "text": "Элита состояла из вольных рыбарей и двоих-троих сборщиков податей, увлёкшись идеями учителя, они забросили своё непотребное занятие."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a81f1a46-c952-42c0-9a32-dd688e1fd07b",
                                "sense_id": "e7155259-c3d7-3f2c-844e-beafa180d228",
                                "text": "Но слушай: в родине моей // Между пустынных рыбарей // Наука дивная таится. // Под кровом вечной тишины, // Среди лесов, в глуши далёкой // Живут седые колдуны; // К предметам мудрости высокой // Все мысли их устремлены; // Всё слышит голос их ужасный, // Что было и что будет вновь, // И грозной воле их подвластны // И гроб и самая любовь."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "848c62c7-640b-4a79-aed1-4c51567d780d",
                        "source_entry_id": "1811f407-04b5-3f47-986b-39c2bb483a30",
                        "source_sense_id": "e7155259-c3d7-3f2c-844e-beafa180d228",
                        "target_lang_word": "fisherman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fisherman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fisher, a person engaged in fishing:",
                                            "Any person who attempts to catch fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31367e79-098d-4cc5-a630-4a76bbfd064e",
                                                "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                                "text": "The fisherman casts her line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4b05e09-287b-4383-b771-31d20451538b",
                                                "sense_id": "71637fac-cb77-3961-8a47-fa1677f5e48d",
                                                "text": "Ivor had acquired more than a mile of fishing rights with the house ; he was not at all a good fisherman, but one must do something ; one generally, however, banged a ball with a squash-racket against a wall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fisher, a person engaged in fishing:",
                                            "A person whose profession is catching fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d1bf685-b0fc-4816-9f1c-866a334d9618",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "He is a fisherman, out on a trawler for days at a time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcd61329-58dd-4dcd-af27-48f89ff9a4da",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "I knovv God by Miracle can inſtruct Kings, as he rained Mannah, and raiſed the Apoſtles from letterless Fiſher-men, to learned Metropolitans, and profound Doctours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d192f9a-6d7a-4720-ab27-c29715fc31ea",
                                                "sense_id": "141442af-a78d-30ef-a1a7-f71dd418c113",
                                                "text": "Alienated from the clique society, / A lonely boy finds peace in fishing. / His mother says John this is not the way life's supposed to be. / Don't you see the life that you are missing? / And he says / When I grow up I want to be, / One of the harvesters of the sea. / I think before my days are done, / I want to be a fisherman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                        "entry_id": "2ada41be-e862-3266-a331-53c0281e91f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vessel (boat or ship) used for fishing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51344829-addc-4e31-93eb-aff7c2c14e69",
                                                "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                                "text": "They tortured and put to death English factors in the Spice Islands; they descended upon the fisheries of the North Sea in huge fleets escorted by men-of-war that attacked and sank the fishermen of other nations"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3bd7ca-ff9d-4717-9b91-2d3d1b728d97",
                                                "sense_id": "11a84e57-80ba-3abb-887f-80a84ee82700",
                                                "text": "Such boats should not have been fast, but the better fishermen — particularly John Alden's designs - […] won a big share of the offshore and coastwise races"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d97b220-f02f-4bec-acf5-144fa95a3207",
                        "source_entry_id": "1811f407-04b5-3f47-986b-39c2bb483a30",
                        "source_sense_id": "e7155259-c3d7-3f2c-844e-beafa180d228",
                        "target_lang_word": "fisher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fisher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec6614e6-2994-3812-8742-7b9658b16c8f",
                                        "entry_id": "cd9ab00a-908b-38aa-8834-a8d78ef57291",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who catches fish, especially for a living or for sport; a person engaging in the pastime of fishing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd4ae6fc-5742-40b9-85ca-593f70de4db7",
                                                "sense_id": "ec6614e6-2994-3812-8742-7b9658b16c8f",
                                                "text": "The fishers who live here left for the mainland only days ago as an unseasonable October storm ravaged the islands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fisher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f6a4bc8-02a0-343b-be90-7172065b653d",
                                        "entry_id": "3e134fc9-cbdd-32f7-b9a1-b1023cee04e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A North American marten-like mammal (Pekania pennanti, syn. Martes pennanti), that has thick brown fur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8201c795-8270-42be-800f-2da4a5ba89d6",
                                                "sense_id": "4f6a4bc8-02a0-343b-be90-7172065b653d",
                                                "text": "In many ways the fisher resembles the pine marten, possessing many of the marten's tricks and manners."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "646089f2-d058-48ff-86a4-fa32f53a6312",
                                                "sense_id": "4f6a4bc8-02a0-343b-be90-7172065b653d",
                                                "text": "In the southeastern United States, Krohn et al. (1994) hypothesize that the inverse relationship between captures of fishers and martens by commercial trappers may result from an interaction between competitive displacement of marten by fisher and the avoidance of areas with deep and frequent snowfalls by fishers but not martens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f64fd87-ad93-42ea-a65e-d404752a847b",
                                                "sense_id": "4f6a4bc8-02a0-343b-be90-7172065b653d",
                                                "text": "The term \"forest carnivores\" denotes a smaller group of four species - the marten, fisher, lynx, and wolverine - and is only marginally descriptive, inasmuch as it excludes many carnivores that live in forests, and includes the wolverine, which can thrive in the complete absence of trees."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66577947-d43a-3e90-aba7-47a8bc3ae09f",
                                        "entry_id": "3e134fc9-cbdd-32f7-b9a1-b1023cee04e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fur of specimens of species Pekania pennanti."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
